WEBVTT

00:20.979 --> 00:23.398
- Oh, it's working.
- What?

00:24.232 --> 00:25.900
Is that your phone, Asahi?

00:25.984 --> 00:28.486
No, it's the one I picked up.

00:31.156 --> 00:32.198
Is it recording?

00:32.282 --> 00:33.116
Yes.

00:34.534 --> 00:36.828
I'm pretty sure the camera's working.

00:58.433 --> 00:59.601
Unreal…

01:01.102 --> 01:02.437
There's no one in this town.

01:04.355 --> 01:07.358
Everyone in Tokyo
seems to have disappeared.

01:14.532 --> 01:16.326
We're in Harajuku and no one's here.

01:16.910 --> 01:18.036
Yeah.

01:27.921 --> 01:29.214
What's going on?

01:36.846 --> 01:38.848
There's not a living soul around.

01:38.932 --> 01:40.391
It's been five days now.

01:41.768 --> 01:44.562
Taking another video?
What are you gonna do with them?

01:45.146 --> 01:46.147
Leaving a record.

01:46.856 --> 01:48.399
What's the point?

01:49.484 --> 01:51.194
Someone might see it one day.

01:54.197 --> 01:55.532
And after a little while,

01:56.825 --> 01:58.118
we met someone.

02:00.787 --> 02:01.913
There was this place…

02:02.914 --> 02:04.874
where we were taken to and…

02:06.793 --> 02:09.504
When we got there, we started working.

02:16.845 --> 02:17.804
Okay?

02:28.982 --> 02:30.650
Are you seriously going in there?

02:45.081 --> 02:47.041
It's pitch black in here.

02:50.336 --> 02:51.296
Momoka?

02:52.338 --> 02:53.423
Momoka?

02:54.632 --> 02:55.758
Momoka!

04:29.352 --> 04:31.771
Fifteen minutes remaining.

04:45.994 --> 04:47.245
Kill 'em all.

04:53.209 --> 04:54.210
I…

04:55.044 --> 04:57.797
I can't do this anymore.

04:57.880 --> 04:59.007
We've got no choice.

05:03.011 --> 05:05.638
We'll never be the same again
after killing so many people.

05:08.975 --> 05:10.059
Did you hear me?

05:11.936 --> 05:14.314
Anyone who defies me here is the witch.

05:19.402 --> 05:20.570
Just shoot me then!

05:22.613 --> 05:23.573
That's enough!

05:30.163 --> 05:31.622
This ends now!

05:37.920 --> 05:38.838
You…

05:39.672 --> 05:41.507
You had me tied up the whole time.

05:42.925 --> 05:45.011
When the murder happened,
that's where I was.

05:46.137 --> 05:47.722
So that means that you know that…

05:48.765 --> 05:50.475
That I can't be the witch.

05:54.437 --> 05:57.982
And if you aren't the witch,
you don't need to kill me.

05:58.941 --> 06:02.070
Just work with me
and we'll find the witch!

06:14.082 --> 06:15.249
Arisu!

06:18.086 --> 06:19.212
Stop it!

06:22.548 --> 06:23.883
I know everything!

06:25.593 --> 06:28.179
You're going after Arisu
even though you know he didn't do it.

06:29.472 --> 06:30.890
And that's…

06:30.973 --> 06:32.475
because you're the witch!

06:34.102 --> 06:36.062
Arisu!

06:43.611 --> 06:44.654
Are ya…

06:45.405 --> 06:46.406
the witch?

06:54.539 --> 06:55.540
Yes.

06:56.457 --> 06:57.792
I am the witch.

07:18.938 --> 07:19.897
Go ahead.

07:22.692 --> 07:23.985
Do it!

07:29.907 --> 07:31.242
Well, shoot him!

07:31.325 --> 07:32.660
Aguni is not the witch!

07:35.246 --> 07:37.415
It's a Ten of Hearts game!

07:37.498 --> 07:40.001
It plays with your feelings
and your emotions!

07:40.668 --> 07:42.920
You're not gonna win by killing Aguni.

07:43.004 --> 07:44.922
That's not the way this game works.

07:52.054 --> 07:53.473
I know you're not the witch.

07:54.640 --> 07:55.766
So why then?

07:57.185 --> 07:58.978
You gotta have another reason.

08:00.771 --> 08:02.106
What are you saying?

08:04.233 --> 08:05.693
The one that you killed

08:06.569 --> 08:07.737
wasn't Momoka.

08:09.572 --> 08:10.531
It was Hatter.

08:12.116 --> 08:13.159
What?

08:19.499 --> 08:21.334
I could see it right away in your eyes.

08:22.793 --> 08:25.087
It was as if you lost all hope and…

08:26.464 --> 08:27.548
just gave up.

08:28.341 --> 08:29.634
I had the same feeling…

08:31.219 --> 08:33.012
when I killed my friends.

08:38.518 --> 08:39.894
You're not dumb.

08:40.686 --> 08:43.439
But as soon as you took over,
you wanted to kill everyone.

08:44.398 --> 08:45.775
And that's not like you.

08:47.401 --> 08:49.070
So you…

08:49.153 --> 08:50.988
…had to have another motive.

08:54.242 --> 08:55.993
Ever since I came to the Beach,

08:56.619 --> 08:58.162
I couldn't quite figure it out.

08:59.997 --> 09:01.999
If you had possession of all these guns,

09:02.708 --> 09:05.336
why didn't the militant corps take over
a long time ago?

09:06.254 --> 09:08.005
That never happened until now.

09:09.799 --> 09:10.883
Because in the end,

09:11.968 --> 09:14.345
you weren't against Hatter at all.

09:16.055 --> 09:17.932
Didn't you actually help each other out?

09:20.518 --> 09:22.520
You wanted to make sure that…

09:22.603 --> 09:25.147
scary people like Niragi
don't go ballistic.

09:26.774 --> 09:28.234
You tried to hold them back.

09:37.743 --> 09:38.703
I know…

09:41.080 --> 09:42.832
how close you and Hatter were.

09:42.915 --> 09:44.709
You were best friends, weren't you?

09:48.087 --> 09:49.630
Then, why did you kill him?

09:54.010 --> 09:55.261
I'll tell you why.

09:57.054 --> 10:00.141
Because you could never forgive him
for what he did.

10:02.768 --> 10:06.022
You wanted it all to stop,
but it was too late.

10:11.068 --> 10:13.779
You didn't recognize him anymore,
isn't that right?

10:41.098 --> 10:42.516
These crazy games…

10:44.393 --> 10:45.686
They're gonna continue?

10:50.900 --> 10:55.112
I will create a utopia here.
An oasis.

10:57.490 --> 10:59.950
For all of those out there
who have lost hope…

11:03.954 --> 11:05.706
I offer the possibility

11:06.207 --> 11:07.875
of a better life!

11:11.337 --> 11:13.339
This will be where hope is born.

11:17.176 --> 11:18.302
That's impossible.

11:19.637 --> 11:20.596
Really?

11:24.350 --> 11:26.018
We can do it together.

11:33.693 --> 11:35.486
Hear my words now.

11:36.404 --> 11:38.030
We're all in this together.

11:39.323 --> 11:42.493
We're going to unite
and gather all the cards…

11:43.119 --> 11:45.079
and get back to the world we knew!

11:57.633 --> 11:58.718
Idiots…

11:59.719 --> 12:02.513
thought they could hide
their playing cards from me.

12:24.952 --> 12:25.995
Aguni.

12:30.916 --> 12:32.626
As of this day,

12:35.379 --> 12:38.048
there will be a new rule.

12:46.849 --> 12:49.226
"Death to any traitor."

12:56.192 --> 12:57.902
You don't know anything!

13:06.494 --> 13:07.536
Stop it!

13:23.677 --> 13:24.804
You know nothing.

13:26.972 --> 13:27.973
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

13:38.776 --> 13:39.777
This way.

13:51.664 --> 13:53.290
Congratulations.

14:08.097 --> 14:10.266
That brings back memories.

14:12.101 --> 14:14.478
This place really hasn't changed at all.

14:19.942 --> 14:20.943
Look…

14:23.153 --> 14:24.321
I'm done.

14:27.116 --> 14:29.952
We're losing control of Niragi
and the militant corps.

14:33.956 --> 14:35.624
Let's get rid of the Beach.

14:40.296 --> 14:41.338
Get rid of it?

14:43.757 --> 14:45.885
Every member of the Beach

14:46.552 --> 14:50.097
is consumed with the happiness
that they found there.

14:50.931 --> 14:53.058
Getting back to the old world
by gathering a few cards

14:53.142 --> 14:54.977
was just a lie you came up with.

14:59.356 --> 15:00.441
We need to end this.

15:03.110 --> 15:04.111
So you're…

15:04.945 --> 15:06.488
betraying me, then?

15:13.329 --> 15:15.915
"Death to any traitor," right?

15:18.208 --> 15:20.920
That's the rule of the Beach,
remember that.

15:21.003 --> 15:22.504
The Beach means nothing!

15:23.297 --> 15:24.506
Just stop this.

15:27.301 --> 15:30.971
I wanted to instill hope,
to create a utopia!

15:31.055 --> 15:33.557
It's bullshit, and you know it!

15:34.516 --> 15:36.352
There is no hope here.

15:40.189 --> 15:41.440
This world we're in…

15:43.067 --> 15:44.860
has crushed all hope.

15:55.329 --> 15:56.288
You see,

15:59.208 --> 16:01.460
I used to have friends with me
I could trust.

16:04.505 --> 16:05.923
But all the hope I had…

16:09.134 --> 16:10.469
died along with them.

16:27.444 --> 16:28.904
Sometimes, a king…

16:31.824 --> 16:34.118
is in a position where he has
to make decisions

16:34.201 --> 16:35.619
that are painfully hard.

16:41.208 --> 16:42.710
Like right now,

16:44.294 --> 16:45.379
my friend.

17:09.319 --> 17:11.655
I know what it feels like
to see your friends die.

17:13.198 --> 17:15.993
To kill them, I see it.

17:17.327 --> 17:20.039
You killed your friend.
I see it in your eyes.

17:21.457 --> 17:24.418
And now you just wanna kill everyone here,

17:24.501 --> 17:27.713
because they were the ones
who made your friend crazy.

17:30.674 --> 17:34.928
These painful feelings of yours,
the game master is using all of them.

17:36.680 --> 17:39.641
That's why it's a game of Hearts.
Don't you get that?

17:39.725 --> 17:41.935
Shut up!

17:42.019 --> 17:42.853
Arisu!

17:44.146 --> 17:46.565
So if all of this is true, then…

17:46.648 --> 17:49.860
Aguni wanted to kill everyone
no matter what the game was.

17:51.987 --> 17:53.572
He had you do it.

17:54.323 --> 17:56.867
And we said nothing
and went along with it all.

17:59.119 --> 18:03.248
So, who here is the witch then?

18:04.500 --> 18:05.751
I know who it is.

18:07.753 --> 18:09.213
I know who the real witch is.

18:14.927 --> 18:16.929
A game master…

18:17.012 --> 18:19.473
uses similar characteristics
in every game.

18:22.101 --> 18:23.435
In a game of Hearts,

18:24.478 --> 18:27.356
he usually makes a fool out of everyone.

18:28.857 --> 18:31.610
Difficulty, Seven of Hearts.

18:31.693 --> 18:34.404
A game of betrayal plays with our hearts.

18:34.488 --> 18:35.405
It's bullshit!

18:38.742 --> 18:40.911
It looks like the wolf
is the one that needs to hide!

18:42.538 --> 18:44.164
It might be that…

18:45.958 --> 18:48.043
…there really was a way to end the game…

18:50.003 --> 18:51.964
without having to kill everyone.

18:54.091 --> 18:55.342
A solution where…

18:56.844 --> 18:58.637
nobody has to get hurt,

18:59.555 --> 19:00.889
and no one has to die.

19:02.766 --> 19:05.435
But… that's impossible.

19:06.603 --> 19:08.605
We have to hunt down the witch

19:08.689 --> 19:10.649
and burn them
in the Fire of Judgment, right?

19:11.817 --> 19:13.360
No.

19:22.161 --> 19:24.079
The witch could be right here and…

19:25.455 --> 19:26.832
no one dies.

19:31.336 --> 19:32.462
Because it's…

19:34.214 --> 19:36.758
Momoka. She was the witch all along.

19:51.607 --> 19:54.776
So, wait.
She stabbed herself in the chest?

19:55.903 --> 19:57.112
Yes.

19:58.614 --> 20:01.742
If I were the game master…

20:01.825 --> 20:03.619
…that's what I would come up with.

20:10.042 --> 20:12.711
You're full of shit!

20:12.794 --> 20:14.213
I'm the witch!

20:15.422 --> 20:18.342
You all wanna kill me, right?

20:29.311 --> 20:31.897
Aguni's trying
to take everyone down with him.

21:26.576 --> 21:28.078
Oh, Takeru.

21:32.541 --> 21:33.500
Hey.

21:34.126 --> 21:36.920
Takeru. Takeru.

21:39.381 --> 21:40.465
Takeru!

21:48.807 --> 21:51.018
This Beach made him crazy.

21:51.101 --> 21:52.352
Do you hear me?

21:52.436 --> 21:54.730
You guys made him crazy!

21:58.150 --> 22:00.193
Kill me, I'm the witch!

22:05.365 --> 22:08.201
Listen.
I know how to stop Aguni, trust me!

22:10.203 --> 22:11.705
I'll get his attention, all right?

22:12.289 --> 22:14.041
Burn Momoka in the Fire of Judgment.

22:16.043 --> 22:16.877
Arisu.

22:18.920 --> 22:21.089
This whole thing has to stop now, okay?

22:26.303 --> 22:27.554
Asahi!

22:30.724 --> 22:31.725
Everyone!

22:34.686 --> 22:36.146
I'm the one!

22:36.229 --> 22:38.482
The dealer of this game!

23:10.013 --> 23:11.473
It was a reverse grip.

23:16.853 --> 23:20.816
Fingerprints with a reverse grip
were found on the knife.

23:30.242 --> 23:31.243
That means

23:32.452 --> 23:34.704
that Momoka grabbed
the handle of the knife

23:35.455 --> 23:37.332
and stabbed it through her own chest.

23:45.757 --> 23:47.217
She was the witch.

23:52.264 --> 23:53.890
But why would she do that?

23:54.933 --> 23:56.601
It couldn't have been just for the game.

23:57.561 --> 24:00.772
So Momoka was really…
the game master after all?

24:02.566 --> 24:04.317
And that girl said she was the dealer.

24:07.028 --> 24:09.990
So they were just toying with us
the whole time, then?

24:12.909 --> 24:15.579
So there was never any high power
doing all this?

24:16.455 --> 24:17.497
They were just human?

24:21.501 --> 24:22.752
But it's possible that…

24:24.379 --> 24:26.965
they could've been
controlled by somebody else.

24:33.805 --> 24:34.848
Aguni.

24:38.518 --> 24:39.769
We need to stop this.

24:41.313 --> 24:43.315
No more innocent people have to die.

24:44.691 --> 24:46.151
Too many people have already.

24:50.238 --> 24:54.451
I understand how it feels…
to kill your friends.

24:55.785 --> 24:57.329
But we can't take it out on…

24:58.330 --> 25:00.624
people who are still alive!

25:03.335 --> 25:04.961
We are still alive!

25:06.296 --> 25:08.256
We're all in this together…

25:09.591 --> 25:12.135
and we have to fight to end it all!

25:15.972 --> 25:18.892
I don't want anybody else to die!

25:51.091 --> 25:52.342
The fire is spreading!

25:53.552 --> 25:55.303
Run!

25:58.431 --> 26:01.017
- Hurry! Put her in the Fire of Judgment!
- Hurry, run!

26:12.362 --> 26:13.196
That hurt.

26:19.869 --> 26:22.205
If I could do it all over again,

26:24.874 --> 26:28.461
I'd use this Fire of Judgment
to burn this whole place down!

26:29.170 --> 26:31.339
- Niragi…
- Niragi?

26:33.133 --> 26:36.011
And that will make me the winner!

27:09.461 --> 27:10.337
Get off me!

27:13.840 --> 27:15.759
I'm gonna kill you!

27:31.733 --> 27:33.568
You are dead.

27:33.652 --> 27:36.112
I'll kill you all!

27:58.385 --> 27:59.678
Aguni.

28:09.604 --> 28:12.273
Three minutes
remaining in the game.

28:12.357 --> 28:13.566
We need to hurry!

28:17.696 --> 28:18.655
Grab her legs.

28:18.738 --> 28:20.323
Ready? Now lift!

28:27.038 --> 28:28.248
Come on!

28:29.457 --> 28:31.459
Hurry! Move, move, move!

29:23.553 --> 29:25.013
Congratulations.

29:25.096 --> 29:27.015
GAME CLEARED
CONGRATULATIONS

29:34.439 --> 29:37.859
There is no safe place
for us in this world.

29:43.406 --> 29:46.951
When the first explorers
discovered the north pole,

29:47.035 --> 29:48.995
the world was unspoiled

29:49.078 --> 29:52.040
and spared of the burden of civilization.

29:54.125 --> 29:58.922
And when it is all said and done,
we simply return to the soil.

30:01.800 --> 30:02.967
This land

30:03.593 --> 30:05.720
is a mirror to the world.

30:07.430 --> 30:09.599
I am thankful to this place.

30:12.560 --> 30:13.478
For now…

30:15.146 --> 30:18.358
I'm freer than ever before.

30:44.509 --> 30:46.594
This is the end of our paradise.

30:54.769 --> 30:56.646
So many of us died.

31:17.333 --> 31:18.459
I don't think I…

31:19.502 --> 31:20.795
can ever forgive them.

31:23.047 --> 31:25.425
- Let me go!
- You can't.

31:28.678 --> 31:29.804
But they…

31:30.889 --> 31:32.473
They killed 'em all!

31:33.224 --> 31:34.517
I can't let that go!

31:58.499 --> 31:59.584
Let's stop this.

32:01.586 --> 32:04.255
Everyone here, we're still alive.

32:06.299 --> 32:08.343
And that's all that matters right now.

32:10.845 --> 32:12.138
That's all that matters.

32:13.264 --> 32:14.223
Arisu?

32:15.266 --> 32:16.100
Arisu!

32:34.077 --> 32:35.286
I get it now.

32:41.292 --> 32:42.669
I understand.

32:43.544 --> 32:44.587
Arisu…

33:31.342 --> 33:33.052
You never quit, do you?

33:38.057 --> 33:41.394
I was starting to think
collecting these cards was pointless.

33:41.477 --> 33:43.021
What do you think now?

33:44.439 --> 33:45.732
I'm thinking that…

33:47.108 --> 33:49.777
we still haven't seen
any of the face cards.

33:52.488 --> 33:57.118
And so what is it
the game's controllers want us to see?

34:07.879 --> 34:09.797
- Is it recording?
- Yes.

34:11.132 --> 34:13.760
I'm pretty sure the camera's working.

34:18.014 --> 34:19.307
What is this?

34:20.183 --> 34:22.143
It's a video that Asahi left behind.

34:25.104 --> 34:26.189
Unreal…

34:27.982 --> 34:29.442
There's no one in this town.

34:31.069 --> 34:34.030
Everyone in Tokyo
seems to have disappeared.

34:36.866 --> 34:38.159
And after a little while,

34:39.243 --> 34:40.953
we met someone.

34:43.164 --> 34:44.332
There was this place…

34:45.333 --> 34:47.126
where we were taken to and…

34:49.253 --> 34:51.798
When we got there, we started working.

34:56.094 --> 34:57.470
We helped with…

34:58.513 --> 35:00.640
preparing and executing the games.

35:04.018 --> 35:05.561
Are you seriously going in there?

35:15.238 --> 35:17.323
There are people known as dealers

35:18.074 --> 35:20.118
who help facilitate the games.

35:24.080 --> 35:29.127
Sometimes we actually join the games
or act as taggers.

35:30.503 --> 35:33.005
Everyone thinks
we are just regular players,

35:33.923 --> 35:36.134
and part of our job is to confuse them.

35:37.802 --> 35:38.719
But…

35:39.303 --> 35:42.723
during the games,
we're being watched the entire time,

35:43.683 --> 35:47.436
and we'll be killed if anyone
ever finds out that we're the dealers.

35:49.021 --> 35:52.859
Are you recording again?
What are you gonna do if they find out?

36:12.170 --> 36:15.423
BEWARE OF ELECTROCUTION
TRAIN CABLES ABOVE

36:24.849 --> 36:26.642
Is this where the game master is?

37:15.566 --> 37:16.901
Stop!

37:18.778 --> 37:20.571
They're really going at it!

37:36.504 --> 37:38.172
All right, yes, yes!

37:45.137 --> 37:47.306
DEALER WINS

37:53.396 --> 37:54.480
Who are they?

37:56.941 --> 37:59.443
So these are all the game masters?

38:10.538 --> 38:12.164
So many have died.

38:13.457 --> 38:16.627
I remember one girl around our age.

38:19.380 --> 38:21.173
Our job was…

38:21.757 --> 38:23.926
…to make sure the game went
the way they wanted it,

38:24.510 --> 38:27.221
and we joined in.

38:27.305 --> 38:29.515
And we made sure many players died.

38:30.808 --> 38:32.101
Because of us,

38:33.936 --> 38:35.896
many people die every day.

38:40.318 --> 38:41.902
I can't take this anymore.

38:45.406 --> 38:47.658
We kill people, win the game,

38:48.451 --> 38:49.910
and earn visa days.

38:55.041 --> 38:57.501
We get to live for another two weeks,

38:57.585 --> 38:59.962
but I don't even know
how many people I've…

39:01.839 --> 39:04.091
I can't do it anymore.

39:05.676 --> 39:07.470
Momoka.

39:08.971 --> 39:11.515
This is all a dream.

39:14.352 --> 39:16.145
It's all right.

39:17.146 --> 39:19.190
We're going to wake up
from this nightmare soon.

39:32.370 --> 39:34.622
I want it all to be over…

40:05.027 --> 40:06.195
So this is it.

40:43.732 --> 40:44.859
There it is.

40:51.407 --> 40:56.912
BEWARE OF ELECTROCUTION
TRAIN CABLES ABOVE

43:00.786 --> 43:02.246
I don't believe it.

43:12.506 --> 43:14.800
So you actually
found this place.

43:21.056 --> 43:23.350
I expected no less from you.

43:26.895 --> 43:28.188
Long time no see.

43:31.066 --> 43:32.151
What's going on?

43:34.528 --> 43:38.324
Thanks to you two, I have
all the numbered playing cards right here.

43:39.283 --> 43:40.242
Thank you.

43:42.411 --> 43:44.079
How did you find this place?

43:47.082 --> 43:50.085
It took me a while,
but I figured out that this is actually

43:50.169 --> 43:52.087
the map of a subway station.

44:08.479 --> 44:10.773
So what happens
when we collect all the cards?

44:11.690 --> 44:15.527
I thought coming here
would provide me with an answer.

44:16.654 --> 44:19.740
But I gotta tell you,
I only know one thing.

44:20.532 --> 44:22.868
These people aren't the game masters,
are they?

44:24.328 --> 44:25.371
Right.

44:26.455 --> 44:27.748
What's pretty clear is

44:28.415 --> 44:30.876
they were all killed after our victory.

44:31.543 --> 44:34.838
They're just humans like us,
and the kicker is…

44:36.340 --> 44:37.633
there's someone above them.

44:45.474 --> 44:47.935
So, then… who could they be?

44:49.395 --> 44:50.396
Who knows?

44:51.730 --> 44:52.898
Maybe aliens.

44:55.442 --> 44:56.735
Maybe God.

45:05.452 --> 45:08.163
SPECIAL URGENT BROADCAST

45:12.042 --> 45:15.462
Congratulations to all players.

45:19.174 --> 45:20.300
Huh?

45:21.844 --> 45:22.761
Oh.

45:27.099 --> 45:28.267
Mira.

45:30.561 --> 45:32.479
Except for the face cards,

45:33.021 --> 45:35.482
you've all completed the numbered games

45:36.066 --> 45:37.901
and emerged victorious.

45:38.944 --> 45:41.613
And the prize of these sweet victories

45:41.697 --> 45:44.575
was the sacrifice of many lives.

45:49.163 --> 45:50.205
I wonder…

45:51.498 --> 45:54.501
just how many
of your close friends have died?

45:59.465 --> 46:01.049
Do you remember…

46:03.761 --> 46:05.554
…the ones who were shot in the head?

46:08.932 --> 46:10.768
That girl you burned alive…

46:15.272 --> 46:17.065
The ones struck down by lasers…

46:18.734 --> 46:20.360
Or the ones who drowned?

46:23.155 --> 46:24.865
Help me!

46:24.948 --> 46:26.992
The ones whose heads were blown off?

46:27.701 --> 46:29.244
Your friends.

46:32.206 --> 46:34.333
All that despair you felt…

46:34.416 --> 46:35.584
Karube!

46:35.667 --> 46:39.254
Those gruesome scenes,
you'll never forget them.

46:42.508 --> 46:43.675
And that…

46:44.426 --> 46:46.011
…really touches me.

46:52.226 --> 46:54.144
To all surviving players,

46:55.145 --> 46:56.271
we just wanted

46:57.564 --> 46:59.191
to give you a present.

47:00.734 --> 47:02.820
Going back to our world?

47:05.823 --> 47:07.407
There will be new games!

47:10.285 --> 47:13.956
Let's all play,
and this time with all the face cards!

47:15.499 --> 47:16.792
New games?

47:18.085 --> 47:19.670
I don't hate that idea.

47:21.713 --> 47:26.051
We've got so many more wonderful
and exciting games in store for you all,

47:26.802 --> 47:28.095
so be prepared.

47:30.722 --> 47:32.015
So then…

47:32.850 --> 47:34.351
Is she the game master?

47:36.186 --> 47:38.313
I think I'd rather see an alien up there.

47:39.606 --> 47:42.609
The next stage starts tomorrow,

47:43.610 --> 47:45.445
when the clock strikes noon.

47:46.697 --> 47:48.240
Let's have some fun,

47:49.032 --> 47:50.492
all together!

47:52.160 --> 47:53.996
So we have to fight once again.

47:55.372 --> 47:56.290
Yeah.

47:58.500 --> 47:59.877
But there's one difference.

48:03.422 --> 48:05.883
Now we know what our target looks like.

48:46.882 --> 48:49.551
SHIBUYA CENTER STREET

48:51.386 --> 48:53.305
SHIBUYA STATION

49:33.553 --> 49:35.597
That's where we'll find our answers.
